# Homepage performance

- Keep the homepage server-rendered or static where possible; add client JavaScript only for necessary interaction.
- Preserve accessible labels, contrast, semantic links, and SEO while optimizing.
- Treat Lighthouse Performance 90+ on both mobile and desktop as the green release target.
- Run three audits sequentially per device and report individual scores plus the median in readable text.
- Separate local build measurements from public production measurements; do not call a change shipped until the live site is verified.
- Show Lighthouse results in the terminal or report. Keep machine-readable JSON temporary; do not send JSON files as the human-facing result.
- Do not change analytics or Cloudflare settings as a side effect of a performance audit.
